# Modules the seed carries: exactly what the front end needs before it can
# compile anything, and nothing else.
#
# The bootstrap window is narrow. `warmFrontEnd` in src/runtime/modules/module.c loads
# the compiler's own closure with `sLoadingFrontEnd` set, and only inside that
# window is the seed consulted. Everything the compiler needs AFTER it is
# running -- the rest of std and anything under packages -- is compiled from
# source on demand and cached, so carrying it here only makes the binary
# bigger.
#
# HOW TO REGENERATE THIS LIST. It is the set of modules actually served from
# the seed, measured rather than reasoned about:
#
#     find lib -name __jaicache__ -type d -exec rm -rf {} +
#     JAITHON_TRACE_LOAD=1 ./jaithon run <something> 2>&1 |
#         awk '$1=="load" && $2=="seed" {print $3}'
#
# over a few different programs, unioned. Note the clean has to be `find`:
# caches nest (lib/jaithon/compile/__jaicache__), and removing only the
# top-level ones leaves a warm tree that will under-report by an order of
# magnitude.
#
# A module missing from this list does not degrade anything -- it makes the
# tree unable to compile at all, loudly, at `make seed-check`. That is the
# intended failure: over-inclusion costs size, under-inclusion is caught.
jaithon/ast.jai
jaithon/ast/kinds.jai
jaithon/ast/node.jai
jaithon/ast/operators.jai
jaithon/ast/schema.jai
jaithon/ast/span.jai
jaithon/ast/tree.jai
jaithon/ast/types.jai
jaithon/ast_encode.jai
jaithon/ast_unparse.jai
